ns, we apply trainable modality alignment tensors /u1D416 /u1D454 and /u1D416 /u1D452 to convert /u1D49B /u1D454 and /u1D49B /u1D450 into language embedding tokens /u1D407 /u1D454 ∈ ℝ /u1D48D /u1D454 × /u1D485 ℎ and /u1D407 /u1D450 ∈ ℝ /u1D48D /u1D450 × /u1D485 ℎ , which have the same dimensionality as the nucleotide token embedding space /u1D485 ℎ in the DNA LLM:\n\n<!-- formula-not-decoded -->\n\nWhere ⋅ represents tensor-vector product, /u1D459 /u1D454 and /u1D459 /u1D450 denote the token numbers of gene expression feature and cell type, receptively. Thus, we obtain a sequence of cell context tokens /u1D407 /u1D484/u1D461/u1D465 = /u1D407 /u1D450 /u1D407 /u1D454 . Similarly, the promoter sequence is encoded as /u1D407 /u1D45D using the word embedding of /u1D453 /u1D74D .\n\nConsequently, given the cell context tokens /u1D407 /u1D484/u1D461/u1D465 and a pair of promoter-enhancer sequence /u1D499 /u1D45D /u1D49A , the loss function that maximizes the likelihood of conditional probability /u1D45D /u1D49A /u1D499 /u1D450 /u1D499 /u1D454 /u1D499 /u1D45D is constructed as:\n\n<!-- formula-not-decoded -->\n\nwhere /u1D73D = /u1D74D /u1D753 /u1D416 /u1D454 /u1D416 /u1D450 is the trainable parameter set."}]

