./analysis/screening_run_artifacts_after_prompt_update_20260511/prompt_iteration_runs/prompt_stability_iter1_current_rep1_deepseekv4_3gpu_11472_20260509T125211Z/guideline_pilot_raw_completed.csv:2:benchmark:10,CellPLM: Pre-training of Cell Language Model Beyond Single Cells,"The current state-of-the-art single-cell pre-trained models are greatly inspired by the success of large language models. They trained transformers by treating genes as tokens and cells as sentences. However, three fundamental differences between single-cell data and natural language data are overlooked: (1) scRNA-seq data are presented as bag-of-genes instead of sequences of RNAs; (2) Cell-cell relations are more intricate and important than inter-sentence relations; and (3) The quantity of single-cell data is considerably inferior to text data, and they are very noisy. In light of these characteristics, we propose a new pre-trained model CellPLM , which takes cells as tokens and tissues as sentences. In addition, we leverage spatially-resolved transcriptomic data in pre-training to facilitate learning cell-cell relationships and introduce a Gaussian mixture prior distribution as an additional inductive bias to overcome data limitation. CellPLM is the first single-cell pre-trained transformer that encodes cell-cell relations and it consistently outperforms existing pre-trained and non-pre-trained models in diverse downstream tasks, with 100x times higher inference speed compared to existing pre-trained models.",benchmark_boundary_case,,,,,,,0,"{""paper_type"": ""primary_model_paper"", ""bio_modality_present"": ""yes"", ""text_component_present"": ""no"", ""text_bio_bridge_present"": ""no"", ""primary_exclusion_code"": ""EC2_no_text_component"", ""uncertainty_reason"": ""none"", ""evidence_for_text_component"": ""none"", ""evidence_for_text_bio_bridge"": ""none"", ""evidence_for_generative_model"": ""not_assessed"", ""boundary_case"": ""biological_token_only_boundary"", ""decision_rationale"": ""The abstract describes a pre-trained model using cells as tokens and tissues as sentences on single-cell transcriptomic data, with no natural-language text component; thus it fails the text component criterion.""}",primary_model_paper,yes,no,no,EC2_no_text_component,none,none,none,not_assessed,biological_token_only_boundary,"The abstract describes a pre-trained model using cells as tokens and tissues as sentences on single-cell transcriptomic data, with no natural-language text component; thus it fails the text component criterion.","{""paper_type"": ""primary_model_paper"", ""generative_model_present"": ""no"", ""foundation_model_evidence"": ""yes"", ""primary_exclusion_code"": ""EC3_not_generative"", ""uncertainty_reason"": ""none"", ""evidence_for_text_component"": ""not_assessed"", ""evidence_for_text_bio_bridge"": ""not_assessed"", ""evidence_for_generative_model"": ""none"", ""boundary_case"": ""clear_exclude"", ""decision_rationale"": ""The paper proposes a pre-trained transformer for cell representation learning without any generative mechanism; it is an encoder-only model focused on encoding cell-cell relations, not generating sequences or biological outputs.""}",primary_model_paper,no,yes,EC3_not_generative,none,not_assessed,not_assessed,none,clear_exclude,"The paper proposes a pre-trained transformer for cell representation learning without any generative mechanism; it is an encoder-only model focused on encoding cell-cell relations, not generating sequences or biological outputs.",EXCLUDE,EXCLUDE,False
./analysis/screening_run_artifacts_after_prompt_update_20260511/prompt_iteration_runs/prompt_stability_iter1_current_rep1_deepseekv4_3gpu_11472_20260509T125211Z/guideline_pilot_raw_completed.csv:4:        Large-scale foundation models have recently opened a new avenue to artificial general intelligence for life sciences, showing great promise in the analysis of single-cell transcriptomic data. Nevertheless, such challenges as the tremendous number of signaling regions, extreme data sparsity, and the nearly binary nature of single-cell epigenomic data have prevented the construction of a foundation model for epigenomics thus far, though it is evident that abundant epigenomic properties such as chromatin accessibility provide more decisive insights into cell states than transcriptomics, shaping the chromatin regulatory landscapes that control transcription in distinct cell types. Here, we introduce EpiAgent, the first foundation model for single-cell chromatin accessibility data, pretrained on a manually curated large-scale Human-scATAC-Corpus that is comprised of approximately 5 million cells and 35 billion tokens. EpiAgent encodes chromatin accessibility patterns of cells as concise “cell sentences,” and employs a bidirectional attention mechanism to capture cellular heterogeneity behind regulatory networks. With comprehensive benchmarks, we demonstrate that EpiAgent excels in typical downstream tasks, including unsupervised feature extraction, supervised cell type annotation, and data imputation. By incorporating external embeddings, EpiAgent facilitates the prediction of cellular responses to both out-of-sample stimulated and unseen genetic perturbations, as well as reference data integration and query data mapping. By simulating the knockout of key cis-regulatory elements, EpiAgent enables in-silico treatment for cancer analysis. We further extended zero-shot capabilities of EpiAgent, allowing direct cell type annotation on newly sequenced datasets without additional training.",benchmark_boundary_case,,,,,,,3,"{""paper_type"": ""primary_model_paper"", ""bio_modality_present"": ""yes"", ""text_component_present"": ""no"", ""text_bio_bridge_present"": ""no"", ""primary_exclusion_code"": ""EC2_no_text_component"", ""uncertainty_reason"": ""none"", ""evidence_for_text_component"": ""none"", ""evidence_for_text_bio_bridge"": ""none"", ""evidence_for_generative_model"": ""not_assessed"", ""boundary_case"": ""clear_exclude"", ""decision_rationale"": ""The abstract describes a foundation model for single-cell chromatin accessibility data using 'cell sentences' as biological tokens, with no mention of natural-language text, prompts, or text-bio alignment, so it fails the text component criterion.""}",primary_model_paper,yes,no,no,EC2_no_text_component,none,none,none,not_assessed,clear_exclude,"The abstract describes a foundation model for single-cell chromatin accessibility data using 'cell sentences' as biological tokens, with no mention of natural-language text, prompts, or text-bio alignment, so it fails the text component criterion.","{""paper_type"": ""primary_model_paper"", ""generative_model_present"": ""no"", ""foundation_model_evidence"": ""yes"", ""primary_exclusion_code"": ""EC3_not_generative"", ""uncertainty_reason"": ""none"", ""evidence_for_text_component"": ""not_assessed"", ""evidence_for_text_bio_bridge"": ""not_assessed"", ""evidence_for_generative_model"": ""none"", ""boundary_case"": ""clear_exclude"", ""decision_rationale"": ""EpiAgent employs bidirectional attention (encoder-only) for epigenomic data, without any generative mechanism such as decoder, autoregressive, or diffusion; thus it is not a generative model.""}",primary_model_paper,no,yes,EC3_not_generative,none,not_assessed,not_assessed,none,clear_exclude,"EpiAgent employs bidirectional attention (encoder-only) for epigenomic data, without any generative mechanism such as decoder, autoregressive, or diffusion; thus it is not a generative model.",EXCLUDE,EXCLUDE,False
./analysis/screening_run_artifacts_after_prompt_update_20260511/prompt_iteration_runs/prompt_stability_iter1_current_rep1_deepseekv4_3gpu_11472_20260509T125211Z/guideline_pilot_raw_completed.csv:5:benchmark:9,Generative pretraining from large-scale transcriptomes: Implications for single-cell deciphering and clinical translation,"Exponential accumulation of single-cell transcriptomes poses great challenge for efficient assimilation. Here, we present an approach entitled tGPT towards integration of 22.3 million single-cell transcriptomes by modeling gene expression rankings as generative pretraining task. tGPT is conceptually simple in that it autoregressively models the ranking of a gene in the context of its preceding neighbors. We demonstrated the high performance of tGPT on a range of fundamental single-cell analysis tasks and novel applications on bulk tissues. The single-cell clusters and cell lineage trajectories derived from tGPT are highly aligned with known cell labels and states. The feature patterns of tumor bulk tissues learned by tGPT are associated with a wide range of genomic alteration events, prognosis and treatment outcome of immunotherapy. tGPT represents a new analytical paradigm for integrating and deciphering massive amount of transcriptome data and it will facilitate the interpretation and clinical translation of single-cell transcriptomes.",benchmark_boundary_case,,,,,,,6,"{""paper_type"": ""primary_model_paper"", ""bio_modality_present"": ""yes"", ""text_component_present"": ""no"", ""text_bio_bridge_present"": ""no"", ""primary_exclusion_code"": ""EC2_no_text_component"", ""uncertainty_reason"": ""none"", ""evidence_for_text_component"": ""none"", ""evidence_for_text_bio_bridge"": ""none"", ""evidence_for_generative_model"": ""not_assessed"", ""boundary_case"": ""clear_exclude"", ""decision_rationale"": ""tGPT autoregressively models gene expression rankings, a biological-token modeling task with no natural-language text, prompts, captions, or explicit text-bio alignment. Thus text_component_present=no, leading to exclusion under EC2.""}",primary_model_paper,yes,no,no,EC2_no_text_component,none,none,none,not_assessed,clear_exclude,"tGPT autoregressively models gene expression rankings, a biological-token modeling task with no natural-language text, prompts, captions, or explicit text-bio alignment. Thus text_component_present=no, leading to exclusion under EC2.","{""paper_type"": ""primary_model_paper"", ""generative_model_present"": ""yes"", ""foundation_model_evidence"": ""yes"", ""primary_exclusion_code"": ""none"", ""uncertainty_reason"": ""none"", ""evidence_for_text_component"": ""not_assessed"", ""evidence_for_text_bio_bridge"": ""not_assessed"", ""evidence_for_generative_model"": ""autoregressively models the ranking of a gene in the context of its preceding neighbors as a generative pretraining task"", ""boundary_case"": ""biological_token_only_boundary"", ""decision_rationale"": ""The abstract describes tGPT, an autoregressive generative model pretrained on 22.3 million single-cell transcriptomes, with evidence of broad applicability. However, it operates on gene expression rankings, not natural language text, placing it at a biological-token-only boundary.""}",primary_model_paper,yes,yes,none,none,not_assessed,not_assessed,autoregressively models the ranking of a gene in the context of its preceding neighbors as a generative pretraining task,biological_token_only_boundary,"The abstract describes tGPT, an autoregressive generative model pretrained on 22.3 million single-cell transcriptomes, with evidence of broad applicability. However, it operates on gene expression rankings, not natural language text, placing it at a biological-token-only boundary.",EXCLUDE,PASS,False
