./analysis/screening_run_artifacts_after_prompt_update_20260511/full_runs/nemotron3_super_120b_fp8_review_pipeline_all4027_current_watchdog_20260511T1116Z/job_11581/guideline_pilot_results_partial.csv:98:                Advances in AI have introduced several strong models in computational pathology to usher it into the era of multi-modal diagnosis, analysis, and interpretation. However, the current pathology-specific visual language models still lack capacities in making diagnosis with rigorous reasoning paths as well as handling divergent tasks, and thus challenges of building AI Copilots for real scenarios still exist. Here we introduce TeamPath, an AI system powered by reinforcement learning and router-enhanced solutions based on large-scale histopathology multimodal datasets, to work as a virtual assistant for expert-level disease diagnosis, patch-level information summarization, and cross-modality generation to integrate transcriptomic information for the clinical usage. We also collaborate with pathologists from Yale School of Medicine to demonstrate that TeamPath can assist them in working more efficiently by identifying and correcting expert conclusions and reasoning paths. Overall, TeamPath can flexibly choose the best settings according to the needs, and serve as an innovative and reliable system for information communication across different modalities and experts.","['T Liu', 'W Xuan', 'H Wu', 'P Humphrey', 'M DiStasio']",2025.0,arXiv preprint arXiv …,,https://arxiv.org/abs/2511.17652,['google_scholar'],1,[],1,,crossref_title,186.0,,51,"{""paper_type"": ""primary_model_paper"", ""bio_modality_present"": ""yes"", ""text_component_present"": ""unclear"", ""text_bio_bridge_present"": ""unclear"", ""primary_exclusion_code"": ""none"", ""uncertainty_reason"": ""mixed_signals"", ""evidence_for_text_component"": ""none"", ""evidence_for_text_bio_bridge"": ""none"", ""evidence_for_generative_model"": ""not_assessed"", ""boundary_case"": ""thin_abstract_boundary"", ""decision_rationale"": ""The abstract introduces TeamPath as a multimodal pathology system but does not explicitly describe natural-language text input/output or text-conditioned generation, leaving the presence of a substantive text component and text-bio bridge unclear.""}",primary_model_paper,yes,unclear,unclear,none,mixed_signals,none,none,not_assessed,thin_abstract_boundary,"The abstract introduces TeamPath as a multimodal pathology system but does not explicitly describe natural-language text input/output or text-conditioned generation, leaving the presence of a substantive text component and text-bio bridge unclear.","{""paper_type"": ""primary_model_paper"", ""generative_model_present"": ""yes"", ""foundation_model_evidence"": ""unclear"", ""primary_exclusion_code"": ""none"", ""uncertainty_reason"": ""none"", ""evidence_for_text_component"": ""not_assessed"", ""evidence_for_text_bio_bridge"": ""not_assessed"", ""evidence_for_generative_model"": ""cross-modality generation to integrate transcriptomic information"", ""boundary_case"": ""clear_include"", ""decision_rationale"": ""The abstract describes TeamPath as enabling cross-modality generation, indicating a generative architecture, and introduces a primary model built on large-scale multimodal pathology data.""}",primary_model_paper,yes,unclear,none,none,not_assessed,not_assessed,cross-modality generation to integrate transcriptomic information,clear_include,"The abstract describes TeamPath as enabling cross-modality generation, indicating a generative architecture, and introduces a primary model built on large-scale multimodal pathology data.",UNCERTAIN,PASS,True,"{""paper_type"": ""primary_model_paper"", ""bio_modality_present"": ""yes"", ""text_component_present"": ""unclear"", ""text_bio_bridge_present"": ""unclear"", ""generative_model_present"": ""unclear"", ""foundation_model_evidence"": ""unclear"", ""primary_exclusion_code"": ""none"", ""uncertainty_reason"": ""mixed_signals"", ""evidence_for