./analysis/screening_run_artifacts_after_prompt_update_20260511/full_runs/nemotron3_super_120b_fp8_review_pipeline_all4027_current_watchdog_20260511T1116Z/job_11581/guideline_pilot_results_partial.csv:149:3524,scgpt-spatial: Continual pretraining of single-cell foundation model for spatial transcriptomics. bioRxiv,scgptspatial continual pretraining of singlecell foundation model for spatial transcriptomics biorxiv,,,,,"Spatial transcriptomics has emerged as a pivotal technology for profiling gene expression of cells within their spatial context. The rapid growth of publicly available spatial data presents an opportunity to further our understanding of microenvironments that drive cell fate decisions and disease progression. However, existing foundation models, largely pretrained on single-cell RNA sequencing (scRNA-seq) data, fail to resolve the spatial relationships among samples or capture the unique distributions from various sequencing protocols. We introduce scGPT-spatial, a specialized foundation model for spatial transcriptomics continually pretrained on our previously published scGPT scRNA-seq foundation model. We also curate SpatialHuman30M, a comprehensive spatial transcriptomics dataset comprising of 30 million spatial transcriptomic profiles, encompassing both imaging- and sequencing-based protocols. To facilitate integration, scGPT-spatial introduces a novel MoE (Mixture of Experts) decoder that adaptively routes samples for protocol-aware decoding of gene expression profiles. Moreover, scGPT-spatial employs a spatially-aware sampling strategy and a novel neighborhood-based training objective to better capture spatial co-localization patterns among cell states within tissue. Empirical evaluations demonstrate that scGPT-spatial robustly integrates spatial data in mulit-slide and multi-modal settings, and effectively supports cell-type deconvolution and contextualized missing gene expression imputation, outperforming many existing methods. The scGPT-spatial codebase is publicly available at https://github.com/bowang-lab/scGPT-spatial.","['C Wang', 'H Cui', 'A Zhang', 'R Xie', 'H Goodarzi', 'B Wang']",2025.0,,,,['google_scholar'],1,[],1,s2_title,,,,79,"{""paper_type"": ""primary_model_paper"", ""bio_modality_present"": ""yes"", ""text_component_present"": ""no"", ""text_bio_bridge_present"": ""no"", ""primary_exclusion_code"": ""none"", ""uncertainty_reason"": ""none"", ""evidence_for_text_component"": ""none"", ""evidence_for_text_bio_bridge"": ""none"", ""evidence_for_generative_model"": ""not_assessed"", ""boundary_case"": ""clear_exclude"", ""decision_rationale"": ""The abstract describes a spatial transcriptomics foundation model with no mention of natural language text or text-bio alignment; thus lacks a substantive text component and text-bio bridge.""}",primary_model_paper,yes,no,no,none,none,none,none,not_assessed,clear_exclude,The abstract describes a spatial transcriptomics foundation model with no mention of natural language text or text-bio alignment; thus lacks a substantive text component and text-bio bridge.,"{""paper_type"": ""primary_model_paper"", ""generative_model_present"": ""yes"", ""foundation_model_evidence"": ""yes"", ""primary_exclusion_code"": ""none"", ""uncertainty_reason"": ""none"", ""evidence_for_text_component"": ""not_assessed"", ""evidence_for_text_bio_bridge"": ""not_assessed"", ""evidence_for_generative_model"": ""novel MoE (Mixture of Experts) decoder that adaptively routes samples for protocol-aware decoding of gene expression profiles"", ""boundary_case"": ""clear_include"", ""decision_rationale"": ""The abstract describes a MoE decoder for decoding gene expression profiles, indicating a generative architecture. It also notes continual pretraining on a large spatial transcriptomics dataset, providing foundation-model evidence.""}",primary_model_paper,yes,yes,none,none,not_assessed,not_assessed,novel MoE (Mixture of Experts) decoder that adaptively routes samples for protocol-aware decoding of gene expression profiles,clear_include,"The abstract describes a MoE decoder for decoding gene expression profiles, indicating a generative architecture. It also notes continual pretraining on a large spatial transcriptomics dataset, providing foundation-model evidence.",EXCLUDE,PASS,False,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,EXCLUDE|PASS,primary_model_paper,yes,no,no,yes,yes,,,,,,,"The abstract describes a spatial transcriptomics foundation model with no mention of natural language text or text-bio alignment; thus lacks a substantive text component and text-bio bridge. | The abstract describes a MoE decoder for decoding gene expression profiles, indicating a generative architecture. It also notes continual pretraining on a large spatial transcriptomics dataset, providing foundation-model evidence.",EXCLUDE,EC2_no_text_component,,EXCLUDE,EC2_no_text_component,,False
./analysis/screening_run_artifacts_after_prompt_update_20260511/full_runs/nemotron3_super_120b_fp8_review_pipeline_all4027_current_watchdog_20260511T1116Z/job_11581/guideline_pilot_results_partial.csv:150:3525,Genegpt: augmenting large language models with domain tools for improved access to biomedical information. arXiv,genegpt augmenting large language models with domain tools for improved access to biomedical information arxiv,,,,,"While large language models (LLMs) have been successfully applied to various tasks, they still face challenges with hallucinations. Augmenting LLMs with domain-specific tools such as database utilities can facilitate easier and more precise access to specialized knowledge. In this paper, we present GeneGPT, a novel method for teaching LLMs to use the Web APIs of the National Center for Biotechnology Information (NCBI) for answering genomics questions. Specifically, we prompt Codex to solve the GeneTuring tests with NCBI Web APIs by in-context learning and an augmented decoding algorithm that can detect and execute API calls. Experimental results show that GeneGPT achieves state-of-the-art performance on eight tasks in the GeneTuring benchmark with an average score of 0.83, largely surpassing retrieval-augmented LLMs such as the new Bing (0.44), biomedical LLMs such as BioMedLM (0.08) and BioGPT (0.04), as well as GPT-3 (0.16) and ChatGPT (0.12). Our further analyses suggest that: (1) API demonstrations have good cross-task generalizability and are more useful than documentations for in-context learning; (2) GeneGPT can generalize to longer chains of API calls and answer multi-hop questions in GeneHop, a novel dataset introduced in this work; (3) Different types of errors are enriched in different tasks, providing valuable insights for future improvements.","['Q Jin', 'Y Yang', 'Q Chen', 'Z Lu']",,,,,['google_scholar'],1,[],1,s2_title,,,,80,"{""paper_type"": ""application_wrapper"", ""bio_modality_present"": ""yes"", ""text_component_present"": ""yes"", ""text_bio_bridge_present"": ""yes"", ""primary_exclusion_code"": ""application_wrapper"", ""uncertainty_reason"": ""none"", ""evidence_for_text_component"": ""prompt Codex to solve the GeneTuring tests"", ""evidence_for_text_bio_bridge"": ""teaching LLMs to use the Web APIs of the National Center for Biotechnology Information (NCBI) for answering genomics questions"", ""evidence_for_generative_model"": ""not_assessed"", ""boundary_case"": ""wrapper_boundary"", ""decision_rationale"": ""The abstract describes GeneGPT as a method to augment an existing LLM (Codex) with NCBI API use for genomics question answering, indicating an application wrapper around a pre‑existing LLM that bridges text queries to biological data.""}",application_wrapper,yes,yes,yes,application_wrapper,none,prompt Codex to solve the GeneTuring tests,teaching LLMs to use the Web APIs of the National Center for Biotechnology Information (NCBI) for answering genomics questions,not_assessed,wrapper_boundary,"The abstract describes GeneGPT as a method to augment an existing LLM (Codex) with NCBI API use for genomics question answering, indicating an application wrapper around a pre‑existing LLM that bridges text queries to biological data.","{""paper_type"": ""application_wrapper"", ""generative_model_present"": ""no"", ""foundation_model_evidence"": ""unclear"", ""primary_exclusion_code"": ""application_wrapper"", ""uncertainty_reason"": ""none"", ""evidence_for_text_component"": ""not_assessed"", ""evidence_for_text_bio_bridge"": ""not_assessed"", ""evidence_for_generative_model"": ""none"", ""boundary_case"": ""none"", ""decision_rationale"": ""The abstract presents GeneGPT as a method for teaching existing LLMs (Codex) to use NCBI APIs via in‑context learning and tool augmentation, not as a new generative architecture. Therefore it is an application wrapper around an existing LLM.""}",application_wrapper,no,unclear,application_wrapper,none,not_assessed,not_assessed,none,none,"The abstract presents GeneGPT as a method for teaching existing LLMs (Codex) to use NCBI APIs via in‑context learning and tool augmentation, not as a new generative architecture. Therefore it is an application wrapper around an existing LLM.",EXCLUDE,EXCLUDE,False,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,EXCLUDE|EXCLUDE,application_wrapper,yes,yes,yes,no,unclear,application_wrapper,,,,,,"The abstract describes GeneGPT as a method to augment an existing LLM (Codex) with NCBI API use for genomics question answering, indicating an application wrapper around a pre‑existing LLM that bridges text queries to biological data. | The abstract presents GeneGPT as a method for teaching existing LLMs (Codex) to use NCBI APIs via in‑context learning and tool augmentation, not as a new generative architecture. Therefore it is an application wrapper around an existing LLM.",EXCLUDE,application_wrapper,,EXCLUDE,application_wrapper,,False
