./analysis/screening_run_artifacts_after_prompt_update_20260511/full_runs/nemotron3_super_120b_fp8_review_pipeline_all4027_current_watchdog_20260511T1116Z/job_11581/guideline_pilot_results_partial.csv:193:3536,LangCell: Language-Cell 737 Pre-training for Cell Identity Understanding,langcell languagecell 737 pretraining for cell identity understanding,,,,,"Cell identity encompasses various semantic aspects of a cell, including cell type, pathway information, disease information, and more, which are essential for biologists to gain insights into its biological characteristics. Understanding cell identity from the transcriptomic data, such as annotating cell types, has become an important task in bioinformatics. As these semantic aspects are determined by human experts, it is impossible for AI models to effectively carry out cell identity understanding tasks without the supervision signals provided by single-cell and label pairs. The single-cell pre-trained language models (PLMs) currently used for this task are trained only on a single modality, transcriptomics data, lack an understanding of cell identity knowledge. As a result, they have to be fine-tuned for downstream tasks and struggle when lacking labeled data with the desired semantic labels. To address this issue, we propose an innovative solution by constructing a unified representation of single-cell data and natural language during the pre-training phase, allowing the model to directly incorporate insights related to cell identity. More specifically, we introduce $\textbf{LangCell}$, the first $\textbf{Lang}$uage-$\textbf{Cell}$ pre-training framework. LangCell utilizes texts enriched with cell identity information to gain a profound comprehension of cross-modal knowledge. Results from experiments conducted on different benchmarks show that LangCell is the only single-cell PLM that can work effectively in zero-shot cell identity understanding scenarios, and also significantly outperforms existing models in few-shot and fine-tuning cell identity understanding scenarios.","['S Zhao', 'J Zhang', 'Y Luo', 'Y Wu', 'Z Nie']",,,,,['google_scholar'],1,[],1,s2_title,,,,89,"{""paper_type"": ""primary_model_paper"", ""bio_modality_present"": ""yes"", ""text_component_present"": ""yes"", ""text_bio_bridge_present"": ""yes"", ""primary_exclusion_code"": ""none"", ""uncertainty_reason"": ""none"", ""evidence_for_text_component"": ""texts enriched with cell identity information"", ""evidence_for_text_bio_bridge"": ""constructing a unified representation of single-cell data and natural language during the pre-training phase"", ""evidence_for_generative_model"": ""not_assessed"", ""boundary_case"": ""clear_include"", ""decision_rationale"": ""The abstract describes LangCell as a pre‑training framework that jointly models single‑cell transcriptomics and natural‑language texts enriched with cell identity information, establishing a substantive text‑bio bridge.""}",primary_model_paper,yes,yes,yes,none,none,texts enriched with cell identity information,constructing a unified representation of single-cell data and natural language during the pre-training phase,not_assessed,clear_include,"The abstract describes LangCell as a pre‑training framework that jointly models single‑cell transcriptomics and natural‑language texts enriched with cell identity information, establishing a substantive text‑bio bridge.","{""paper_type"": ""primary_model_paper"", ""generative_model_present"": ""unclear"", ""foundation_model_evidence"": ""yes"", ""primary_exclusion_code"": ""none"", ""uncertainty_reason"": ""generative_status_unclear"", ""evidence_for_text_component"": ""not_assessed"", ""evidence_for_text_bio_bridge"": ""not_assessed"", ""evidence_for_generative_model"": ""none"", ""boundary_case"": ""generative_boundary"", ""decision_rationale"": ""The abstract describes a pre-training framework for cross-modal understanding but does not mention a decoder, autoregressive, or other generative mechanism. It provides evidence of broad pre-training and zero-shot transfer, supporting foundation-model evidence.""}",primary_model_paper,unclear,yes,none,generative_status_unclear,not_assessed,not_assessed,none,generative_boundary,"The abstract describes a pre-training framework for cross-modal understanding but does not mention a decoder, autoregressive, or other generative mechanism. It provides evidence of broad pre-training and zero-shot transfer, supporting foundation-model evidence.",PASS,UNCERTAIN,True,"{""paper_type"": ""primary_model_paper"", ""bio_modality_present"": ""yes"", ""text_component_present"": ""yes"", ""text_bio_bridge_present"": ""yes"", ""generative_model_present"": ""no"", ""foundation_model_evidence"": ""yes"", ""primary_exclusion_code"": ""none"", ""uncertainty_reason"": ""none"", ""evidence_for_text_component"": ""texts enriched with cell identity information"", ""evidence_for_text_bio_bridge"": ""constructing a unified representation of single-cell data and natural language during the pre-training phase"", ""evidence_for_generative_model"": ""none"", ""boundary_case"": ""clear_include"", ""decision_rationale"": ""Abstract shows alignment of single-cell data with natural language texts for pre-training, confirming text component and bridge, but lacks any explicit generative mechanism (e.g., decoder, autoregressive, diffusion), so generative_model_present is no.""}",primary_model_paper,yes,yes,yes,no,yes,none,none,texts enriched with cell identity information,constructing a unified representation of single-cell data and natural language during the pre-training phase,none,clear_include,"Abstract shows alignment of single-cell data with natural language texts for pre-training, confirming text component and bridge, but lacks any explicit generative mechanism (e.g., decoder, autoregressive, diffusion), so generative_model_present is no.",PASS|UNCERTAIN,primary_model_paper,yes,yes,yes,no,yes,,,texts enriched with cell identity information,constructing a unified representation of single-cell data and natural language during the pre-training phase,none,clear_include,"Abstract shows alignment of single-cell data with natural language texts for pre-training, confirming text component and bridge, but lacks any explicit generative mechanism (e.g., decoder, autoregressive, diffusion), so generative_model_present is no.",EXCLUDE,EC3_not_generative,,EXCLUDE,EC3_not_generative,,False
./analysis/screening_run_artifacts_after_prompt_update_20260511/full_runs/nemotron3_super_120b_fp8_review_pipeline_all4027_current_watchdog_20260511T1116Z/job_11581/guideline_pilot_results_partial.csv:194:3540,scGPT: Towards Building a Foundation Model for Single-Cell Multi-omics Using Generative Pretraining,scgpt towards building a foundation model for singlecell multiomics using generative pretraining,,,,,"Generative pre-trained models have achieved remarkable success in various domains such as natural language processing and computer vision. Specifically, the combination of large-scale diverse datasets and pre-trained transformers has emerged as a promising approach for developing foundation models. Drawing parallels between linguistic constructs and cellular biology — where texts comprise words, similarly, cells are defined by genes — our study probes the applicability of foundation models to advance cellular biology and genetics research. Utilizing the burgeoning single-cell sequencing data, we have pioneered the construction of a foundation model for single-cell biology, scGPT, which is based on generative pre-trained transformer across a repository of over 33 million cells. Our findings illustrate that scGPT, a generative pre-trained transformer, effectively distills critical biological insights concerning genes and cells. Through the further adaptation of transfer learning, scGPT can be optimized to achieve superior performance across diverse downstream applications. This includes tasks such as cell-type annotation, multi-batch integration, multi-omic integration, genetic perturbation prediction, and gene network inference. The scGPT codebase is publicly available at https://github.com/bowang-lab/scGPT.","['H Cui', 'M Li', 'Y Zhang']",,,,,['google_scholar'],1,[],2,s2_title,,,,90,"{""paper_type"": ""primary_model_paper"", ""bio_modality_present"": ""yes"", ""text_component_present"": ""unclear"", ""text_bio_bridge_present"": ""unclear"", ""primary_exclusion_c