./data/screening_codex_full_2026-07-06/role_logs/scope_reviewer/batch_0136.stderr.log:3001:{"results":[{"record_id":"rec_001081","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_text_component","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract presents a new multimodal framework for pathology images and RNA-seq survival prediction. It uses scGPT as a biological component, but does not describe a substantive text or language component.","evidence_snippet":"“pathology images” and “genomic (e.g., bulk RNA-seq)” with “scGPT” adapted for bulk RNA-seq."},{"record_id":"rec_001082","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_substantive_text_bio_bridge","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is an original model-transfer study for bio-language models across DNA, mRNA, and protein modalities. It does not establish a text-to-biology bridge or any natural-language component.","evidence_snippet":"“bio-language foundation models” and “adaptation of existing DNA and protein bio-language models for mRNA-focused tasks”."},{"record_id":"rec_001083","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_substantive_text_bio_bridge","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The paper introduces pretrained Transformer models over single-cell gene expression with masked gene-expression pretraining. This is a biological language-model paper, but the abstract does not support a substantive text-bio bridge.","evidence_snippet":"“pretrained ... Transformer models” and “masked gene expression pretraining objective” on “50 million human cells”."},{"record_id":"rec_001084","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_text_component","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract describes a DeepSurv survival model built from ctDNA and clinical features. No text or language component is described.","evidence_snippet":"“ctDNA sequencing assays” and “Features associated with overall survival ... incorporated into a deep-learning network (DeepSurv)”."},{"record_id":"rec_001085","paper_type":"application_wrapper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a tooling paper for interpreting and steering an existing genomic language model, not a new candidate model. The abstract centers on SAEs applied to Nucleotide Transformer activations.","evidence_snippet":"“Tools to Interpret, Audit, and Steer Genomic Language Models” and “SAEs trained on Nucleotide Transformer activations”."},{"record_id":"rec_001086","paper_type":"application_wrapper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract describes using a masked autoencoder to extract MRI features for clustering and subtyping. This is an application of an existing model, not a new text-bio candidate model.","evidence_snippet":"“Radiomic features were extracted using Masked Auto-Encoder (MAE)” and “used the four structural modalities”."},{"record_id":"rec_001087","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_text_component","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is an original analysis integrating scRNA-seq with Mendelian randomization to identify a therapeutic target. The abstract does not describe any text or language component.","evidence_snippet":"“integrated MS genome-wide association study (GWAS) data, single-cell transcriptomics (scRNA-seq), eQTL, and pQTL data”."},{"record_id":"rec_001088","paper_type":"review_editorial","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"unclear","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"text_bio_bridge_unclear","decision_rationale":"The abstract is a broad review of predictive analytics for chronic respiratory diseases, not a candidate model paper. It mentions NLP among reviewed techniques, but does not establish a substantive text-bio bridge.","evidence_snippet":"“This explores the integration of big data in predictive analytics” and mentions “natural language processing (NLP)” among techniques."}]}

